# Bali in Bengaluru — project rules for AI assistants

**Read `HANDOVER.md` in the repo root first** — it is the complete brief — and then
**`docs/JOURNAL.md`**, the project's memory: every decision, problem solved and
lesson learned, in order. Do not undo a decision recorded there without raising it.
Its private half is in the sealed vault (`bash tools/vault.sh show`, key `memory`).
This file is the quick-reference version. `AGENTS.md` is the same entry point for
any other AI tool.

## What this is
A campaign hub website for the "Bali in Bengaluru" cultural festival by Param
Foundation. Plain **HTML + CSS + vanilla JS**, no framework, no build step, no
dependencies. Hosted on GitHub Pages (auto-deploys on push to `main`).
Live: https://bali-in-blr.paramfoundation.org

## File map
- `index.html` — content & structure (sections marked with HTML comments; each has an `id`)
- `styles.css` — all styling; **design tokens are in `:root` at the top**; responsive `@media` at the bottom
- `main.js` — behaviour + the `CONFIG` data-bridge object at the very top
- `data/events.json`, `data/partners.json` — local stand-ins for Google Sheets
- `assets/logo.svg` — the festival logo (`assets/title.svg` is the wordmark alone, used
  by the hero `h1` only); inlined as the `.logo` component wherever the
  name is a heading or brand mark (HANDOVER §5)
- `docs/BRIDGE-SETUP.md`, `docs/apps-script/Code.gs` — the backend bridge
- `tools/sync-images.sh` — pulls Google Drive event images from the sheet into `assets/drive/`
- `docs/ANOTHER-MACHINE.md`, `tools/doctor.sh` — working from the drive on a new computer

## Architecture
Data comes from **Google Sheets via a Google Apps Script Web App** ("the bridge").
The bridge is live: signup/volunteer forms save through it and the calendar reads
real dates from the schedule sheet (`CONFIG.SCHEDULE_URL`), falling back to
`data/events.json`. See HANDOVER §3–4.

## Rules
- Keep it **dependency-free** vanilla JS/CSS. Do not add frameworks, build tools, or
  npm packages without a strong, stated reason.
- Styling goes in `styles.css` using classes + `:root` tokens. No inline styles.
- Content edits go in `index.html`; data-driven content goes in `data/*.json` (later the Sheet).
- Always `esc()` any sheet/user-supplied value before inserting into HTML (XSS).
- **Privacy/compliance (Param Foundation):** personal data (emails/phones) may live
  only in approved systems (Google Workspace / Zoho). Never store PII in the repo,
  never send it to unapproved third parties, never expose personal rows on the public
  page — aggregates only. Keep the signup consent checkbox and purpose text (DPDP Act 2023).
- Prefer the Google + Zoho stack for any new integrations.
- Conventions: dates `DD MMM YYYY`, currency INR (₹), Indian English. Festival title
  is exactly "Bali in Bengaluru". As a heading or brand mark it is the inline logo
  (`assets/logo.svg`; the hero `h1` alone uses `assets/title.svg`) with `.sr-only`
  text; inside a sentence it stays text. Never type it as display type or load it
  as an `<img>`.
- After changing CSS/JS, bump the `?v=` query on their `<link>`/`<script>` tags in
  `index.html` for cache-busting.
- Run locally with a server (`python3 -m http.server 8000`), not `file://`, because
  the page `fetch()`es `data/*.json`.
- Event images: staff paste a Google Drive link in the sheet's image column. Run
  `bash tools/sync-images.sh` and commit `assets/drive/` whenever one is added or changed.
- When a change solves a real problem or reverses a decision, add an entry to
  `docs/JOURNAL.md` so the next session inherits it.
- Commit and push at the end of every change. If a push fails with `HTTP 400` /
  `the remote end hung up unexpectedly`, run `git config http.postBuffer 157286400`
  once (the repo's `.git/config` already sets it on the drive). Newly pushed files
  can 404 on the CDN for a minute after the Pages build succeeds — reload first.
